From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:29:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvkms, nvidia-drm: a change of the RGB range in place shuts
 the head down first

On a GeForce GTX 1060 (580 legacy, EVO 2) with Kodi's "Use limited colour
range" on and the TV in limited range (Hades issue 17), the interface had
crushed blacks after every start of Kodi, and turning the setting off and on
again did not change it; the end of a video, with its change of the refresh
rate, made it right. In the kernel log the start and the end of the video
look the same: nvidia-drm asks for limited range (Broadcast RGB "Limited
16:235", hadesColorRangeLimited of KAPI), KAPI makes a mode set of it, and
NVKMS writes an AVI InfoFrame that says limited range (PB3 0x88 to 0x84).

Read in NVKMS: both are mode sets of the head, and both send the same
HEAD_SET_PROCAMP method with range compression (nvUpdateCurrent...Evo(),
from the same proposed attributes as the AVI InfoFrame); no other writer of
the procamp ran in between (a flip with new HDR state would have written the
AVI InfoFrame again, which the log of every InfoFrame does not show). What
differs is how the head is set: at Kodi's start the console's mode is kept,
and an HDMI TMDS head whose hardware heads and timings stay is set again in
the update that shuts it down (the glitchless mode set), its raster running
on; at the end of the video its timings changed. The picture says that in
place the range of the head did not change, although the methods were
sent; why the hardware did not take it is not known.

NVKMS now treats such a head as incompatible with its new configuration
(IsProposedModeSetStateOneApiHeadIncompatible()) when its RGB range changes
with the same pixel clock, raster and protocol: it is shut down in an
update of its own first, as a DisplayPort or an HDMI FRL head always is,
and starts again with its new range. The display sees the signal go and
come back once, where it was kept before: at Kodi's start with the setting
on (Kodi's first mode set has the property already), at each change of the
setting, and where Dolby Vision starts or ends at the same refresh rate
with "Limited 16:235" (the tunnel is full range). A head whose timings
change, an FRL head and a head that is turned on or off take NVKMS's path
as before; with Broadcast RGB at "Automatic" (the default) the range never
changes and nothing does.

The kernel's log says what was done, not what was asked: NVKMS says when a
head is shut down first for its range ("Hades: head N (HDMI-0, head M of
nvidia-drm): the RGB range goes from full to limited range with the raster
as it is: ..."), and when the range compression of a head is written
("Hades: head N (HDMI-0): the range compression of the head is now on: it
sends RGB in limited range (16-235)"), from a mode set, a flip with new HDR
state or an attribute. nvidia-drm's line says that limited range was asked
of NVKMS, instead of "the head compresses the range".

The same as in 580 (nvidia-legacy-open-9069): the mode set path of 615 is the
same, and nothing there says that Turing and later take the range in place
either (not known; no report).

Tested on the host: HadesColorRangeChangesInPlace() of each tree, extracted
as it is, 11 of 11 cases (the start at the console's mode, the setting off,
the range kept, a new pixel clock, 60 to 50 Hz at the same clock, 24 Hz, FRL,
TMDS to FRL, a head turned off, no hardware head), 5 of 5 mutations caught;
the NVKMS core of both trees built with the image's compiler, no new
warning. nvidia-drm only changes the text of a line: not built here. Not
run on a GPU: that the head shut down first comes back with its range
compressed on the GTX 1060 is what the end of the video showed, not a
measurement of this change.

Made again for 620.70.06: the code around it changed there; the change itself is
the same, with the names and types of that release.
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c |  2 +-
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-evo.c          | 46 ++++++++++++++
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-modeset.c      | 70 +++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 117 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
index a2e310b..4367194 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-modeset.c
@@ -600,7 +600,7 @@ nv_drm_atomic_apply_modeset_config(struct drm_device *dev,
             if (head_config->modeSetConfig.hadesColorRangeLimited) {
                 NV_DRM_DEV_LOG_INFO(
                     nv_dev,
-                    "Hades: head %u (%s): RGB in limited range (16-235), as Broadcast RGB asks: the head compresses the range, and the AVI InfoFrame says limited range where the display can select it (the default range otherwise)",
+                    "Hades: head %u (%s): RGB in limited range (16-235) asked of NVKMS, as Broadcast RGB asks, and the AVI InfoFrame says limited range where the display can select it (the default range otherwise); nvidia-modeset says when the range compression of its head is on, and when the head is shut down first for it",
                     head, connector->name);
             } else if (connector_state->hdmi.broadcast_rgb ==
                        DRM_HDMI_BROADCAST_RGB_LIMITED) {
diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-evo.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-evo.c
index 2e12839..532fbd6 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-evo.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-evo.c
@@ -2890,6 +2890,47 @@ void nvUpdateCoreFid(
     pDevEvo->hal->SetCoreFid(pDispEvo, apiHead, pUpdateState);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Hades: the kernel's log says when the range of the pixels that a head sends
+ * changes, as the head is programmed with it (HEAD_SET_PROCAMP: range
+ * compression on for limited range, off for full range), so that a log can
+ * tell what the head was set to send from what was asked of it (nvidia-drm's
+ * "Broadcast RGB" line) and from what the AVI InfoFrame says. Written once per
+ * change; the hardware takes it with the update of the head that follows.
+ */
+static void HadesLogProcAmpRange(const NVDispEvoRec *pDispEvo,
+                                 const NvU32 head,
+                                 const NVDispHeadStateEvoRec *pHeadState,
+                                 const NVT_COLOR_RANGE oldRange)
+{
+    const NvBool limited = (pHeadState->procAmp.colorRange == NVT_COLOR_RANGE_LIMITED);
+    const char *format;
+
+    if (pHeadState->procAmp.colorRange == oldRange) {
+        return;
+    }
+
+    switch (pHeadState->procAmp.colorFormat) {
+    case NVT_COLOR_FORMAT_RGB:      format = "RGB"; break;
+    case NVT_COLOR_FORMAT_YCbCr444: format = "YCbCr 4:4:4"; break;
+    case NVT_COLOR_FORMAT_YCbCr422: format = "YCbCr 4:2:2"; break;
+    case NVT_COLOR_FORMAT_YCbCr420: format = "YCbCr 4:2:0"; break;
+    default:                        format = "an unknown format"; break;
+    }
+
+    nvEvoLogDisp(pDispEvo, EVO_LOG_INFO,
+                 "Hades: head %u (%s): the range compression of the head is now %s: it sends %s in %s",
+                 head,
+                 (pHeadState->pConnectorEvo != NULL) ?
+                     pHeadState->pConnectorEvo->name : "no connector",
+                 limited ? "on" : "off",
+                 format,
+                 limited ? "limited range (16-235)" :
+                     ((pHeadState->timings.yuv420Mode == NV_YUV420_MODE_SW) ?
+                          "full range (the 4:2:0 of NVKMS's headSurface makes its own range)" :
+                          "full range"));
+}
+
 void nvUpdateCurrentHardwareColorFormatAndRangeEvo(
     NVDispEvoPtr pDispEvo,
     const NvU32 head,
@@ -2899,6 +2940,8 @@ void nvUpdateCurrentHardwareColorFormatAndRangeEvo(
     NVDevEvoPtr pDevEvo = pDispEvo->pDevEvo;
     NVDispHeadStateEvoRec *pHeadState = &pDispEvo->headState[head];
     const NVConnectorEvoRec *pConnectorEvo = pHeadState->pConnectorEvo;
+    /* Hades: what the head had, for the kernel's log (HadesLogProcAmpRange()) */
+    const NVT_COLOR_RANGE hadesOldRange = pHeadState->procAmp.colorRange;
 
     nvAssert(pConnectorEvo != NULL);
 
@@ -3025,6 +3068,9 @@ void nvUpdateCurrentHardwareColorFormatAndRangeEvo(
     nvAssert(!((pHeadState->pixelDepth == NVKMS_PIXEL_DEPTH_18_444) &&
                (pHeadState->procAmp.colorRange == NVT_COLOR_RANGE_LIMITED)));
 
+    /* Hades: the range that the head sends, when it changes */
+    HadesLogProcAmpRange(pDispEvo, head, pHeadState, hadesOldRange);
+
     // Set the procamp head method
     pDevEvo->hal->SetProcAmp(pDispEvo, head, pUpdateState);
 }
diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-modeset.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-modeset.c
index 87b5ed2..a126ac5 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-modeset.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-modeset.c
@@ -2654,6 +2654,70 @@ static NvBool IsCurrentMultiTileConfigOneApiHeadIncompatible(
     return FALSE;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Hades: the RGB range of an api-head changes while its raster stays as it is
+ * (the same pixel clock, raster and protocol: no change of timings starts the
+ * head again). KAPI asks for limited range with nvidia-drm's "Broadcast RGB"
+ * ("Limited 16:235", hadesColorRangeLimited), and for NVKMS's own range again
+ * with "Automatic" or "Full" and while the Dolby VSIF goes out. Such a head
+ * went through the glitchless mode set (shut down and set again in one
+ * update, its raster running on): the AVI InfoFrame said the new range at
+ * once, but on a GeForce GTX 1060 (580, EVO 2) the picture stayed in the
+ * old range until a later mode set changed its timings (Hades issue 17:
+ * full range on the cable said to be limited, crushed blacks on a TV in
+ * limited range; Kodi's start and its setting turned off and on again, both
+ * at the mode the console had, did not change it; the end of a video, with a
+ * change of the refresh rate, did), although the mode set had sent the same
+ * HEAD_SET_PROCAMP method. Why the hardware did not take it in place is not
+ * known. The head is shut down first, in an update of its own, as a
+ * DisplayPort or an HDMI FRL head always is, so that it starts again with its
+ * new range: the display sees the signal go and come back once, where the
+ * console's mode is kept. A head whose timings change, an FRL head (always
+ * shut down first) and a head that is turned on or off keep NVKMS's path.
+ */
+static NvBool HadesColorRangeChangesInPlace(
+    const NVDispEvoRec *pDispEvo,
+    const NvU32 apiHead,
+    const NVDpyEvoRec *pDpyEvo,
+    const NVProposedModeSetStateOneApiHead *pProposedApiHead,
+    const NVDispApiHeadStateEvoRec *pApiHeadState)
+{
+    const NVHwModeTimingsEvo *pNew = &pProposedApiHead->timings;
+    const NVHwModeTimingsEvo *pOld = &pApiHeadState->timings;
+
+    if (nvDpyIdListIsEmpty(pProposedApiHead->dpyIdList) ||
+        (pProposedApiHead->hwHeadsMask == 0x0) ||
+        (pProposedApiHead->attributes.color.range ==
+         pApiHeadState->attributes.color.range)) {
+        return FALSE;
+    }
+
+    if ((pNew->protocol == NVKMS_PROTOCOL_SOR_HDMI_FRL) ||
+        (pOld->protocol == NVKMS_PROTOCOL_SOR_HDMI_FRL) ||
+        (pNew->protocol != pOld->protocol) ||
+        (pNew->pixelClockHz != pOld->pixelClockHz) ||
+        (pNew->rasterSize.x != pOld->rasterSize.x) ||
+        (pNew->rasterSize.y != pOld->rasterSize.y) ||
+        (pNew->rasterSyncEnd.x != pOld->rasterSyncEnd.x) ||
+        (pNew->rasterSyncEnd.y != pOld->rasterSyncEnd.y) ||
+        (pNew->rasterBlankEnd.x != pOld->rasterBlankEnd.x) ||
+        (pNew->rasterBlankEnd.y != pOld->rasterBlankEnd.y) ||
+        (pNew->rasterBlankStart.x != pOld->rasterBlankStart.x) ||
+        (pNew->rasterBlankStart.y != pOld->rasterBlankStart.y)) {
+        return FALSE;
+    }
+
+    nvEvoLogDisp(pDispEvo, EVO_LOG_INFO,
+                 "Hades: head %u (%s, head %u of nvidia-drm): the RGB range goes from %s to %s range with the raster as it is: the head is shut down first and set again, so that its new range goes out on the link (set in place, a head kept its old range)",
+                 nvGetPrimaryHwHeadFromMask(pApiHeadState->hwHeadsMask),
+                 pDpyEvo->pConnectorEvo->name, apiHead,
+                 (pApiHeadState->attributes.color.range ==
+                  NV_KMS_DPY_ATTRIBUTE_COLOR_RANGE_LIMITED) ? "limited" : "full",
+                 (pProposedApiHead->attributes.color.range ==
+                  NV_KMS_DPY_ATTRIBUTE_COLOR_RANGE_LIMITED) ? "limited" : "full");
+    return TRUE;
+}
+
 /*!
  * Determine if display devices driven by head are incompatible with newly
  * activated display devices.
@@ -2704,6 +2768,12 @@ IsProposedModeSetStateOneApiHeadIncompatible(
         return TRUE;
     }
 
+    /* Hades: the RGB range of the head changes in place (issue 17) */
+    if (HadesColorRangeChangesInPlace(pDispEvo, apiHead, pDpyEvo,
+                                      pProposedApiHead, pApiHeadState)) {
+        return TRUE;
+    }
+
     for (NvU32 tmpApiHead = 0; tmpApiHead < pDevEvo->numApiHeads; tmpApiHead++) {
         const NVProposedModeSetStateOneApiHead *pTmpProposedApiHead =
             &pProposedDisp->apiHead[tmpApiHead];
